From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ops <ops@local>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 21:07:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] feat: partial ME degradation with per-DC Direct fallback
 and ME recovery

Ports patches 0002 (PR #732, partial ME degradation) and 0003 (migrate
per-DC Direct-fallback sessions back to Middle-End) from 3.4.25 to 3.5.7.

- pool_status: admission_coverage_snapshot, admission_ready_partial_cast and
  admission_ready_for_target_dc; readiness is tracked per DC and address family
- pool_init: partial DC coverage no longer blocks startup
- admission gate: partial readiness keeps the gate open in Middle mode instead
  of a global cutover to Direct; per-DC transition logs and gauges
- authenticated session dispatch: a session goes to Direct only when its own
  target DC has no live ME writer
- direct relay: such sessions return to Middle-End by staggered reconnect once
  the DC stays ready for me_direct_to_me_recovery_hysteresis_secs (default 10)
- metrics: telemt_me_admission_configured_dcs, telemt_me_admission_ready_dcs,
  telemt_me_partial_degradation_active
- config: me_direct_to_me_recovery_enabled (default true),
  me_direct_to_me_recovery_hysteresis_secs (default 10)

Layout changes versus 3.4.25: session dispatch lives in proxy/authenticated.rs,
readiness in pool_status/status_snapshot.rs, metrics in metrics/render,
the transport log in maestro/runtime_startup.rs.
